# Unified Interface Primitives

Business modules own data, state, permissions, actions, and domain semantics.
The Design System owns rendering. Modules may only provide typed presentation adapters.

## Timeline

- Timeline is a Design System primitive.
- All timeline-like, chronological, audit-rail, history, activity, and process-step interfaces must use `src/components/timeline/Timeline.tsx`.
- Modules may map domain data to `TimelineEntry`; they must not render their own rails, connectors, markers, cards, grouping, or timeline empty states.
- Reject any change that introduces a second timeline renderer.

## Kanban

- Kanban is a Design System primitive.
- All status-lane and workflow-board interfaces must use `src/components/kanban/KanbanBoard.tsx`.
- Modules may provide columns, cards, permissions, actions, and transition callbacks; they must not render their own board, columns, headers, counters, cards, or Kanban empty states.
- Reject any change that introduces a second Kanban renderer.

### Active operational stages vs Archive SSOT

- Workflow Kanban adapters must show **active operational stages only**.
- Terminal / archived / cancelled / rejected / received-closed states must **not** be Kanban columns when the module has (or is adding) an Archive/Completed panel as SSOT for those records.
- Adapters must not keep duplicate terminal lanes that only mirror the archive.
- Pre-closure waiting states that are still operational (e.g. WO `completed`, DI `approved` / `deferred`) may remain on the board.
- New boards (PM, permits, etc.) must follow the same split from day one.
- DS tones such as `closed` / `cancelled` may remain for **badges**; they must not justify terminal board columns when Archive exists.
- No change to the `KanbanBoard` primitive API for this split — adapters own column lists and card filters.

### Forbidden in adapters

- Column icons
- Per-column empty copy (`column.empty`) — use board `emptyColumnLabel` from `common.kanban.emptyColumn`
- `headerBadge` or any trailing badge on the code row
- JSX, `className`, or Tailwind in card/column data
- Terminal lanes that only duplicate an Archive panel

### Required slot semantics

Fixed card anatomy (board-owned): accent → code → title → subtitle → description → badges → meta → actions.

| Data | Slot |
|------|------|
| Priority / urgency / status / origin / safety | `badges` |
| Dates / people | `meta` (with Lucide icon references) |
| Entity links (DI↔WO, …) | `link` |
| Asset / supplier / source line | `subtitle` |
| Longer body text | `description` |

Missing optional fields omit the node; they must never invent an alternate layout.

## Extending the registry

- Before building a reusable interface pattern, search for an existing shared primitive and extend it.
- When a new application-wide interface primitive is established, add it to this rule with its canonical renderer path and adapter boundary.
- Keep shared visual behavior, accessibility, responsive layout, and interaction chrome inside the primitive.
- Do not move business fetching, workflow rules, IPC, or domain mutations into Design System primitives.

## AssetPicker

- AssetPicker is a Design System primitive.
- All asset/equipment selection surfaces (DI, WO, and later PM, Inspection, LOTO,
  Failure Reporting, Inventory Reservation, Reliability) must use
  `src/components/assets/AssetPicker.tsx`.
- Modules may pass value, onChange, error, disabled, and context prefill;
  they must not render their own asset search box, 2-char gates, result lists,
  or scan chrome.
- Reject any change that introduces a second asset/equipment picker for identity selection.

### Required behavior (owned by the primitive)

- Open with suggestions (recent for current user, else frequent); no min-char gate
- Search from the first character; accent-insensitive and case-insensitive
- Search fields: code, name, serial, QR/barcode/alias (via external ids)
- Rich rows: code (prominent) + name + org path + optional status; never name-only
- Highlight matching substrings in code and name
- Unique exact code match + Enter selects immediately without showing the list
- Keyboard: Arrow navigation, Enter select, Escape close
- Hardware Scan-QR affordance inside the picker
- Server-side filtering only; do not preload the full asset catalog

### Forbidden in modules

- Inline `searchAssets` comboboxes / duplicated debounce gates
- Min-character gates before showing suggestions
- Name-only result rows
- Module-specific alternate pickers named EquipmentPicker for asset identity selection
  (`EquipmentSearchSelect` remains for reference catalogs only — class/family/org options,
  not asset identity search)
